   "properties": {
    "Node name for S&R": "Note"
   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "Kroma is a Krea2-based OPD model. This graph starts at 1024x1024, 8 steps, CFG 1.0, Euler and the simple scheduler. The vendor recommends 8-12 steps and CFG 1.0-1.5; the native Krea2 Flux sampling shift mu=1.15 is preserved without a model-sampling patch. The negative branch zeros the positive conditioning, as in the official samples. Plain Euler at CFG 1.0 skips the unconditional call. Auto selects the existing krea2 family and Ulysses on a configured pair; BF16 and INT8 do not enable SAGE automatically. Pure Ulysses on two GPUs matched stock one-GPU references for BF16 and local INT8 at 1024x1024, plus BF16 2x refinement. Manual uly2+fsdp at batch 1 also matched for BF16/local INT8 text-to-image and BF16 2x refinement. Batch-2 dp2+fsdp remains CHECK for stock fidelity; keep the default batch 1 and auto topology. LoRA remains untested. See docs/VALIDATION.md#evidence-kroma for measured scope and limits. Reference-image conditioning requires single; padded ring and hybrid retain the Krea2 waiver boundary. Expects kroma-v0.3.1-turbo-opd.safetensors in models/diffusion_models, qwen3vl_4b_bf16.safetensors in models/text_encoders (CLIP type krea2), and qwen_image_vae.safetensors in models/vae. Use detailed natural-language prompts. The graph uses stock conditioning without a prompt extension. The first-use identity gate checks its scoped loading paths; it does not certify output quality or every topology. Pinned model card: https://huggingface.co/lodestones/Kroma/blob/734ec29814972997fa29a1cd313863a2e5e9921c/README.md . Sampling and refinement recipe: https://huggingface.co/lodestones/Kroma/resolve/734ec29814972997fa29a1cd313863a2e5e9921c/samples/output_00001.png"
   ],
   "title": "DGX Monarch | Kroma v0.3.1 BF16 text to image"
  },
